---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { contact, hrefs } from "../config/site";

/* ============================================================
   JVG SHIPPING PROCESS — customer instruction page.
   noIndex: this is a hand-out link Joe texts/emails to sellers,
   not a page meant to be found in search (matches live's
   "noindex, follow"). Deliberately NOT listed on /sitemap/ and
   not linked from nav. If @astrojs/sitemap is ever added,
   exclude /jvg-shipping-process/ there too.

   The FedEx account number and the Fraser Drive shipping address
   are operational facts — keep them EXACTLY as on the live page.
   (The shipping address differs from the site-config contact
   address on purpose; do not swap in contact.address.)
   ============================================================ */

const SHIP_TO = "47 North Fraser Drive East, Mesa, AZ 85203";
const FEDEX_ACCT = "541950800";
---

<Layout
  title="JVG Shipping Process"
  description="Step-by-step instructions for shipping your guitar to Joe's Vintage Guitars: free packing and shipping on my FedEx account, full insurance, and payment before you leave the counter."
  canonical="/jvg-shipping-process/"
  noIndex={true}
>
  <section class="ship-title-bar">
    <div class="ship-inner"><h1>JVG Shipping Process</h1></div>
  </section>

  <section class="ship-body">
    <div class="ship-inner">
      <p class="ship-lede">
        Selling your guitar to me from out of state is simple, secure, and you will see your payment before you
        even leave the FedEx counter. Hundreds of sellers have done this; their 5-star reviews are on
        <a href={hrefs.googleReviews} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Maps</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="ship-callout">
        <ul>
          <li>You pay nothing for packing or shipping. It all goes on my FedEx account.</li>
          <li>Your guitar is fully insured under our private musical-instrument policy.</li>
          <li>Payment is sent the moment you text me the FedEx drop-off receipt.</li>
          <li>I&rsquo;m on text the whole time. If anything is unclear, message me at <a href={hrefs.sms}>{contact.phone}</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 1</span> Send Me Your Info</h2>
      <p>
        Text or email me your preferred email address and a photo of your driver&rsquo;s license. The license
        photo is strictly for fraud prevention; it confirms the sale on both sides. If you&rsquo;re not
        comfortable sharing it, that&rsquo;s fine, we&rsquo;ll simply send your payment after the guitar arrives
        and is verified instead of at the counter.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 2</span> Pack the Inside of the Case</h2>
      <p>
        Before heading to FedEx, open the case and fill every bit of empty space so the guitar cannot move at
        all inside it. Use soft materials you have on hand: newspaper, old t-shirts, towels, paper towels, or
        foam. Close the case and shake it vigorously in every direction. If you hear or feel any shifting, add
        more padding.
      </p>
      <div class="ship-warn">
        <strong>Do not use bubble wrap inside the case.</strong> Bubble wrap can react with the nitrocellulose
        lacquer used on vintage guitar finishes and leave permanent marks. Soft cloth, newspaper, and paper
        towels are all safe. Bubble wrap is fine outside the case, just never touching the guitar.
      </div>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 3</span> Take It to FedEx</h2>
      <p>
        Go to an official <strong>FedEx Print &amp; Ship Center</strong>, not a third-party pack-and-ship store
        that carries a FedEx sign. It&rsquo;s a good idea to call ahead and ask if they have a guitar box in
        stock. Phone tip: when the automated menu picks up, just press 7 and it puts you straight through to a
        person at that location.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 4</span> At the Counter</h2>
      <p>
        Snap a photo of the guitar on the counter and text it to me. Then hand it to the FedEx employee, ask
        them to pack it very tightly, and give them this information:
      </p>
      <table class="ship-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>FedEx Account #</th><td>{FEDEX_ACCT}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Charge to Account</th><td>Packaging + Shipping (you pay nothing)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Ship To</th><td>{SHIP_TO}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Shipping Speed</th><td>Cheapest option, unless I&rsquo;ve told you otherwise</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Insurance</th><td>None. Your guitar is already covered under my private policy.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 5</span> Get Paid Before You Leave</h2>
      <p>
        After FedEx scans in the label, they&rsquo;ll hand you the drop-off receipt. Take a photo of it and text
        it to me. The moment I see that receipt, I send payment.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment Options</h2>
      <p>Pick whichever you already trust: PayPal, Venmo, Zelle, Cash App, wire transfer, or a mailed check.</p>
      <p class="ship-note">
        Some apps have daily or per-transfer limits depending on your account. For larger sales, confirm your
        preferred method with me in advance so the payment goes through in one shot.
      </p>

      <h2>Quick Reference Checklist</h2>
      <ul class="ship-check">
        <li>Email address provided</li>
        <li>Driver&rsquo;s license photo sent (optional but recommended)</li>
        <li>Case packed tightly, no bubble wrap</li>
        <li>Called ahead about a guitar box (press 7 to reach a person)</li>
        <li>Official FedEx Print &amp; Ship Center located</li>
        <li>Photo of the guitar on the counter texted to Joe</li>
        <li>FedEx account #{FEDEX_ACCT} given at the counter</li>
        <li>Cheapest shipping selected</li>
        <li>FedEx insurance declined</li>
        <li>Drop-off receipt photo texted to Joe</li>
        <li>Payment method confirmed in advance</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="ship-contact">
        <p><strong>Questions? Text me anytime.</strong></p>
        <p>
          Phone/Text: <a href={hrefs.tel}>{contact.phone}</a><br />
          Email: <a href={hrefs.mailto}>{contact.email}</a><br />
          Shipping Address: {SHIP_TO}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .ship-inner { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .ship-title-bar {
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-dark, #682412);
    padding: 180px 24px 48px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .ship-title-bar h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 54px);
    color: var(--color-brand-cream);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .ship-body { background: #fff; padding: 44px 0 72px; }
  .ship-body p, .ship-body li {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-brand-charcoal);
  }
  .ship-body p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .ship-lede { font-size: 18px !important; }
  .ship-note { font-style: italic; }
  .ship-body a { color: var(--color-brand-rust); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600; }
  .ship-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ship-step {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-bright, #be4b25);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .ship-callout {
    background: var(--color-brand-cream-light, #f9f1de);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .ship-callout ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .ship-callout li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .ship-warn {
    background: #f6e0da;
    border-left: 4px solid #842012;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #5a1a0d;
  }
  .ship-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .ship-table th, .ship-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(62, 42, 20, 0.12);
    color: var(--color-brand-charcoal);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .ship-table th {
    width: 36%;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .ship-check { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 0; }
  .ship-check li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }
  .ship-check li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .ship-contact {
    margin-top: 36px;
    background: var(--color-brand-cream, #eedfc0);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .ship-contact p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .ship-title-bar { padding: 120px 16px 36px; }
    .ship-table th { white-space: normal; width: 40%; }
  }
</style>
